From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:42:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] docs/bpf: describe ordered CPUMAP migration

Document the opt-in map setting, redirect and state kfuncs, source
reservations, GRO completion boundary and retained entry generations.
Explain the offline exception, rebuilding worker affinity after hotplug,
and why a local PASS fallback can bypass outstanding packets.

Require stable domains for active flows and control-plane ingress
quiescence before detach, admission changes or domain reuse. Describe
socket storage as policy input rather than transport completion state,
and call out the added locking and possible GRO aggregation cost.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
